<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 7 November, from 1665 to 1940.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/london" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1665 CE <span class="tih-ago">361 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Oxford Gazette, later the London Gazette, is first published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With the court in Oxford to escape the plague, the first issue of the Oxford Gazette appeared. Renamed the London Gazette, it is the oldest continuously published newspaper in Britain.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1837 CE <span class="tih-ago">189 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A pro-slavery mob kills Elijah Lovejoy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The abolitionist editor Elijah Lovejoy was shot defending his fourth printing press from a mob in Alton, Illinois. His death turned many northerners towards the anti-slavery cause.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1867 CE <span class="tih-ago">159 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marie Curie is born in Warsaw</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Maria Skłodowska was born in Warsaw, then under Russian rule. As Marie Curie she pioneered research on radioactivity and became the first person to win Nobel Prizes in two sciences.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1917 CE <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Bolsheviks seize power in Petrograd</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bolshevik-led Red Guards took key points in Petrograd and stormed the Winter Palace overnight, toppling the Provisional Government. The October Revolution, so called from the Julian calendar, led to the Soviet state.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julian-calendar">Julian calendar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1940 CE <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Tacoma Narrows Bridge collapses</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Four months after opening, the suspension bridge over Puget Sound twisted violently in a 40-mile-per-hour wind and fell into the water. Filmed footage of 'Galloping Gertie' transformed bridge aerodynamics.</p></div></li></ol>
